a-3.3"],"evidence_ids":["link.navier-stokes.lemma-3.3"],"id":"navier-stokes.lemma-3.3","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 3.3: The bilinear time integral","locator":"Lemma 3.3: The bilinear time integral, Section 3.4","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 3.3.** Let $a\\le b$, and let $u,v:[a,b]\\to\\mathcal X$ be continuous. Then for every $t\\in[a,b]$ the map $t'\\mapsto K(t-t')(u(t'),v(t'))$ is integrable on $[a,t]$, and the map $$\nt\\mapsto\\int_a^t K(t-t')(u(t'),v(t'))\\,dt'\n$$ is continuous on $[a,b]$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/nodes/navier-stokes.lemma-3.3","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/nodes/navier-stokes.lemma-3.3","id":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/edges/%5B%22navier-stokes.lemma-3.3%22%2C%22lean.Breakdown.VarConstIntegralStatement%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/edges/%5B%22navier-stokes.lemma-3.3%22%2C%22lean.Breakdown.VarConstIntegralStatement%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/nodes/lean.Breakdown.VarConstIntegralStatement"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/nodes/navier-stokes.lemma-3.3","id":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/edges/%5B%22navier-stokes.lemma-3.3%22%2C%22lean.Breakdown.varConstIntegral%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:362b14f1b2aab30d298ba8bf02c59247aa0632f89b95797cfe399dc62dc2c0d4/edges/%5B%22navier-stokes.lemma-3.3%22%2C%22lean.Breakdown.varConstIntegral%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:362b14f1b2a